TAP version 13
# Subtest: archive HTTP file creation, ZIP validation and extraction persist through host restarts
ok 1 - archive HTTP file creation, ZIP validation and extraction persist through host restarts
  ---
  duration_ms: 100.6708
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: stored and deflated ZIP files preserve binary, UTF-8, empty files and directories
ok 2 - stored and deflated ZIP files preserve binary, UTF-8, empty files and directories
  ---
  duration_ms: 70.2196
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: ZIP parser validates CRC and headers and refuses traversal, duplicate paths, and oversized expansion
ok 3 - ZIP parser validates CRC and headers and refuses traversal, duplicate paths, and oversized expansion
  ---
  duration_ms: 0.3806
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: malicious archive cannot create files outside workspace and unconfirmed extraction does not write
ok 4 - malicious archive cannot create files outside workspace and unconfirmed extraction does not write
  ---
  duration_ms: 9.2979
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: Windows .NET independently reads generated ZIP and our parser reads independently created ZIP
ok 5 - Windows .NET independently reads generated ZIP and our parser reads independently created ZIP
  ---
  duration_ms: 719.9119
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: TAR/PAX round trips binary, Unicode, long paths, empty files/directories and fractional/negative dates
ok 6 - TAR/PAX round trips binary, Unicode, long paths, empty files/directories and fractional/negative dates
  ---
  duration_ms: 5.1852
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: TAR writer uses PAX when modification time exceeds the ustar octal field
ok 7 - TAR writer uses PAX when modification time exceeds the ustar octal field
  ---
  duration_ms: 0.8395
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: independent ustar prefix, GNU long-name, global/local PAX and deletion records determine metadata
ok 8 - independent ustar prefix, GNU long-name, global/local PAX and deletion records determine metadata
  ---
  duration_ms: 1.3096
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: TAR accepts signed historical checksums and safe base-256 sizes/times, rejects negative/unsafe integers
ok 9 - TAR accepts signed historical checksums and safe base-256 sizes/times, rejects negative/unsafe integers
  ---
  duration_ms: 1.0511
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: TAR refuses header checksum errors, malformed octal, truncation and incorrect end records
ok 10 - TAR refuses header checksum errors, malformed octal, truncation and incorrect end records
  ---
  duration_ms: 0.5789
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: PAX rejects malformed byte lengths, delimiters, UTF-8, numeric size/time and sparse metadata
ok 11 - PAX rejects malformed byte lengths, delimiters, UTF-8, numeric size/time and sparse metadata
  ---
  duration_ms: 2.4323
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: TAR rejects unsafe, duplicate, case-colliding and file/directory-colliding paths before extracting
ok 12 - TAR rejects unsafe, duplicate, case-colliding and file/directory-colliding paths before extracting
  ---
  duration_ms: 2.5753
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: TAR enforces per-file, cumulative, container, metadata and entry-count bounds
ok 13 - TAR enforces per-file, cumulative, container, metadata and entry-count bounds
  ---
  duration_ms: 27.8089
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: GZIP writer exchanges binary data with Node and retains Latin-1 names/comments/header CRC and dates
ok 14 - GZIP writer exchanges binary data with Node and retains Latin-1 names/comments/header CRC and dates
  ---
  duration_ms: 2.708
  type: 'test'
  ...
# Subtest: independent GZIP optional extra/name/comment/headerCRC/text fields and concatenated members decode
ok 15 - independent GZIP optional extra/name/comment/headerCRC/text fields and concatenated members decode
  ---
  duration_ms: 0.5751
  type: 'test'
