# Notes installation: closed source and acceptance plan

This audit reads selected source and existing recorded evidence at commit `016ecd175c0700d1a94d5219af6719989a4a6e45`. It executes no application, original helper, syntax check, build or browser. No active repository or Git changes were made. The exact path/byte census is in `dependency-audit-r3.json`; its 52 planned physical proof paths correspond to 55 logical roles and 1,064,898 known stored bytes before two new declarations are authored. The original audit and R2 are preserved. R2 clarifies the difference between an existing path and the future afterimage bytes at that path. R3 adds a second independently identified direct bypass at the old inline8 installation loop; dependency identities and counts stay unchanged.

The eight application transitions are fixed by the unchanged 10,977-byte Notes bundle `64891708â€¦`: server, client and README replace exact existing bytes; core and four tests are additions. All old thirteen Notes tests stay unchanged. The installed app would have 32 non-result files: 30 eligible executable/JSON sources, one README and the separately pinned synthetic JEX binary. The fixed roster has 17 tests, with 23 newly authored top-level groups and 20 separately counted original helper comparisons. The prior finite run passed 92 groups; the first actual Chromium campaign passed 8 cases. Those are historical source-composition results until a fresh committed-source campaign passes.

The root source read sites affected by installation are:

| Reader and location at the audited base | Exact effect and required change |
| --- | --- |
| `scripts/editor-vault-proof-migration.mjs:1702-1758` | Add a separate Notes read group with eight mandatory current afterimages and exactly three before routes. It must authenticate the existing bundle/payloads and fixed selected evidence using its own 64-path/8-MiB budget. Missing identities, unknown identities and arbitrary paths must fail for named Notes targets. Preserve existing common and Archive groups. |
| `scripts/verify-records.mjs:385-410` | The immutable 737-source/937-group block has two newly historical Notes sources: client and server. Add exactly those two allowed paths; routes become 13 and unchanged current rows become 724. Both old 720-source and 737-source inventories bind the same two exact beforeimages. Keep every historical receipt and its counts unchanged. |
| `scripts/verify-records.mjs:819-827` | Workspace requirements bind exactly client, server and README beforeimages. The existing resolver call can route those three exact identities. No registry, source ID, capability ID or gate is rewritten; retain 159 original source IDs and 232 capability IDs. |
| `scripts/verify-followup-records.mjs:145,169` | Both the old inline8 installation loop and focused 69-group loop directly read live Notes paths. Change their expected-byte reads to resolve the exact historical identity first. Keep all8 earlier installation rows, all26 focused Notes rows, three historical shared rows and the separately pinned JEX. Qualify the returned69-group result as historical to the pre-to-do source epoch, without rewriting either receipt. |
| `scripts/verify-notes-inline-followups.mjs:44,102-104` | Its expected reads already use the shared resolver. The old 34 installed rows and eight proposals remain unchanged. New exact Notes routes preserve its old currentExpected bytes while independently requiring the new live afterimages. No reader source change is needed. |
| `scripts/verify-notes-vault-followups.mjs:94,210` | Its shared resolver already handles expected reads. Its inline historical resolver returns the exact earlier currentExpected identity, which can route through the new Notes table. The reconstruction input at line221 is an inert original-stage path, outside the eight live targets. No reader source change is needed. |
| `scripts/verify-notes-layout-value-api-checkpoint.mjs:5,10` | The 720-source/847-group historical check already uses the shared resolver, so the two exact new Notes before routes are sufficient. No receipt or reader source change is needed. |
| `scripts/verify-records.mjs:25-30,198,209,219,728-734` | Older notebook/455 sources already have immutable snapshot bindings. The pinned JEX and oracle metadata do not change. These paths need no new fallback or rebinding. |
| `scripts/editor-vault-proof-migration.mjs:454-536,1732,1746-1754` | Updating the root and focused69 reader changes two mandatory current verifier after pins. Preserve their exact pre-Notes source images and the migration beforeimage in the new Notes group; add only explicit intermediate-epoch routes for those two readers. Keep all existing oldest/middle epochs, seven mandatory current verifiers and existing rejection behavior. |
| `scripts/publication-integrity-controls.mjs:10,84-89,194-228` | Re-pin the exact new root and VM source. Update only the new current epoch's exact 937 route expectations to13/724, preserve all164 existing controls in source history, and run their regression checks plus new Notes controls on the hosted runner. All other clock, Archive, old-epoch and unknown-route checks remain required. |
| `scripts/verify-cloud-publication.mjs:25-111,191` | Re-pin changed reviewed readers and capture the separate Notes proof in one bounded gzip JSON envelope with every exact path, byte count, hash and raw byte payload. This avoids adding dozens of loose files to the existing artifact. Its contents remain independently readable without executing product code. |

There are three distinct existing budgets. The common migration reader is159/160 paths and16MiB. The Archive proof reader is94/96 paths and8MiB. The publication artifact is91/96 files:76 reviewed-source snapshots and15 other roles, with35MiB raw and15MiB ZIP bounds. These budgets must retain their current limits and coverage. The proposed independent Notes group has52 planned physical paths under64 and8MiB; all known individual inputs fit256KiB. One complete Notes envelope would make the publication artifact92/96 files, subject to actual hosted packaging/readback verification. A52-file loose capture would not fit and is excluded from this plan.

The minimal proof group retains eight mandatory live afterimages; the unchanged seventeen source-bundle payloads; the bundle and released original Note source; exact beforeimages of the root, migration and focused69 reader; two new source declarations; nine selected finite metadata roles; and fourteen browser metadata/review roles. The finite before/after roles share one content-addressed payload; the browser before/after/postcheck roles share another. This saves three physical reads, explaining55 logical roles versus52 physical paths. Its read, decode, recheck and summary counts must be closed and independently checked. The large complete browser ZIP stays preserved in its existing public capsule; root proof validation does not need to duplicate or execute it.

Implementation should proceed in this order:

1. Author work-only source declarations, the exact eight application copies and the five root/publication reader changes against the final audited base. Preserve the three before-readers and the complete current controls source. Add the independent Notes resolver/read group and its selected immutable evidence; keep all older experiments, authority files and receipts byte-identical.
2. Add source-only mutation controls for all eight mandatory live sources, all three beforeimages, missing/unknown named identities, declaration closure, both immutable experiment epochs, and exact requirement/937 routing. Independently review the full proposed sources and pins before active copy. The source plan must say that committed behavioral acceptance is pending.
3. Add a closed `verify-notes-installed-cloud.mjs` helper and explicit finite/browser installed scopes, reusing the unchanged reviewed 17-file test roster and eight-case browser spec. Authenticate all32 current Notes files and all8 exact after pins, then require a clean committed checkout and every other eligible Git blob. Preserve all old Flow/Vault, Archive, Windows and experimental modes.
4. Add a two-job standard hosted Windows acceptance workflow with Node24.16 and locked Playwright/Chromium. The finite job must record actual17-file outcomes, all23 new names and20 helper comparisons separately; the browser job must require8 cases,4 real response holds,2 real downloads, one genuineHTTP400 conflict,8 PNGs and8 complete cleanups. Both jobs need independent always-run source postchecks, bounded complete failure artifacts, zero skips/retries and raw evidence preservation.
5. Preserve the old two experimental workflow sources and retire their automatic triggers before installing the eight files. The existing browser experiment triggers on Notes source changes and would otherwise attempt the old baseline composition after installation. Retain their historical/manual definitions and uninstalled scope; do not relabel them as installed runs.
6. After independent review, let the root perform exact active copy and commit/push. Collect actual publication and new installed acceptance evidence, preserve failures before fixing anything, and verify portable local/public backups. A passing installation source check alone cannot mark the installed17-file or browser8 campaign accepted.

No full original application or GUI comparison is established by these finite campaigns. The task helpers remain bounded released-Joplin source comparisons, and the serialized JEX input retains its older separately documented serializer/stub boundary. Feature completeness, browser matrix, security, performance/usability comparison, full parity and superiority remain separate open work.
