  acceptanceScope: options.scope === 'notes-todo-installed' ? 'Fixed17-file Notes roster and92 groups on clean committed32-file Notes sources and8 exact after pins. All23 new names and20 original helper comparisons remain separate, actual HTTP delivery and every other active Git blob are required. Independent always source postcheck is separate. No source installation by collector, original full application/GUI, browser, full-suite, security, parity or superiority acceptance; frozen README describes the reviewed proposal epoch.' : options.scope === 'archive-aes-installed' ? 'Thirteen finite Archive test files and161 groups on committed installed after-images. All62 current Archive files and21 current after pins, every other eligible active Git blob and a separate same-attempt source postcheck are required. Original acquisition is separate from actual comparisons. No app overlay, full Archive suite, browser, production installer validation, parity or superiority acceptance.' : options.scope === 'notes-todo-experiment' ? 'Every current Notes test in a fixed17-file roster under an exact eight-target hosted source composition. Twenty-three authored new groups and twenty original helper comparisons are separate counts. Actual HTTP module delivery, same-attempt full source census, other active Git blobs and an independent source postcheck are mandatory. No production installation, original full application/database/GUI, real browser, security, full parity or superiority acceptance.' : options.scope === 'vault-empty-bin-experiment' ? 'Every current Vault test in a fixed45-file roster on an explicit nine-target source experiment: three runtime changes and six test/helper additions. Twenty initial authored groups, five adjacent groups and two original-library groups are separate source selections; four actual library child operations retain actual dates and are counted separately. All other eligible active sources must match committed Git, source before/after and an independent postcheck must pass. No production installation, actual browser, full-suite, security, parity or superiority acceptance.' : options.scope === 'windows-path-installed' ? 'Five finite Editor Git and Sync WebDAV test files on a clean committed checkout whose three current source images exactly match the reviewed after-image pins. Every eligible active source is Git-blob authenticated; same-attempt source census and a separate committed-source postcheck are required. This collector performs no source installation or composition and does not authenticate a production installer receipt. Full suite, browser, security, parity and superiority remain separate.' : options.scope === 'windows-path-experiment' ? 'Five finite Editor Git and Sync WebDAV test files with a hosted-only three-target source composition: one explicit Sync runtime correction, one Editor physical-path observer correction and one new Windows regression file. Git identifies the committed baseline and inert payloads; composition identifies the active derivative. A separate same-attempt source postcheck is required. Active production integration, full suite, browser acceptance, security, parity and superiority remain open.' : options.scope === 'full-oracle-experiment' ? 'Every current implemented development test with an explicitly composed three-file bsdtar oracle-test overlay. Application runtime sources retain their Git baseline bytes; two oracle loaders and a new helper belong to a new test-dependency epoch. A separate same-attempt composer postcheck remains required. No unchanged-test, historical-DLL, browser, product-parity or superiority acceptance.' : options.scope === 'archive-aes-experiment' ? 'Finite experimental Archive AES and Windows source metadata contracts on an explicitly composed hosted working tree. The Git revision alone describes the baseline and committed overlay payloads; composition provenance identifies the active experimental bytes. Production integration, full Archive acceptance, browser acceptance, full parity and superiority remain open.' : options.scope === 'flow-vault' ? 'Finite Flow and Vault implemented contracts; other applications are not executed.' : 'Current implemented development contracts; every documented original feature and comparative acceptance remain open.',
