Source-only Notes task browser proposal. Not installed, dispatched or executed.

Eight candidate files: spec/config/roster, closed Notes browser helper, fixed
browser source bundle/contract, dedicated workflow, and the exact shared browser
collector Notes dispatch addition. The generic development collector is unchanged.
Read SOURCE-CONTRACT.md and change-authority.json before any active copy.
Every existing shared collector/workflow and every application file is untouched.
The hosted proposal uses the exact36709/558344 post-Archive browser predecessor
and preserves its complete existing Flow/Vault and Archive dispatch body. The
original source proposal is preserved in versions/spec-contract-v1. The exact
revision-error observer now uses string equality after independent spec review.

Four real response holds retain the actual host status/headers/body. Three check
actual disk commit before proceeding; the post-accept list hold also reads disk.
Ordinary enabled-field typing is separate from disabled-control probing (zero).
The actual revision conflict is a genuine saved concurrent write and HTTP400,
followed by explicit reopen/retry. The JEX and resource files are real browser
downloads, with independent native TAR checks and raw portable files retained.

The workflow acquires locked browser tooling before the existing eight-target
Notes composition, then requires the eight real cases and separate always-run
composer plus full browser source postchecks. Full six-directory source census,
seven eligible Notes after pins, separately pinned README, all other Git blobs,
eight PNGs, eight owned cleanup/record objects, four holds and two downloads are
mandatory. The new fixed source bundle binds the exact spec/config/roster,
workflow, original Notes bundle/composer and contract. A15MiB ZIP limit remains.

No local candidate import, syntax check, browser/product test, build or original
execution occurred. All eight proposed scenarios remain unexecuted. Earlier
Notes92 and twenty helper comparisons are distinct actual historical evidence.
No full feature parity or comparative superiority is claimed.
