Notes to-do hosted acceptance tooling -- source authored, unexecuted

Copy only public-candidate/ after independent full source review. Its21 files
are the new workflow, fixed composer, additive generic-collector source, fixed
bundle, and17 inert source/document/review payloads. No active product source
was changed by authoring. The separate reviewed Notes8 source authority remains
335d78a02f53174f8c33a0fe918157418a23eceb80d6ba0e02371f0e8aee32f0.

The composer is a narrowed adaptation of the reviewed Vault hosted pattern.
It is guarded to GitHub-hosted Windows, Node24.16.0 and this repository. It uses
the same-attempt RUNNER_TEMP evidence directory, exact immutable bundle bytes,
committed payload authentication, three exact Git-authenticated before-images,
and five absent addition targets. Only those eight target paths may differ.
Composition performs no tests or original execution and is never installation.
The released Note.ts45302/5f1a source is separately authenticated as committed
and copied into portable evidence before any helper test. Doc/license/source
contracts and r2 review remain inert, authenticated bundle payloads.

The fixed roster is all13 current Notes test files plus the four new files.
All13 existing sources were read in full for compatibility contradictions and
are pinned in current-notes-source-compatibility-review.json. No old test body
was adapted. No full closed object-shape or unsupported-action contradiction
was found; this is source analysis and still requires actual hosted execution.
There are23 newly authored groups and20 planned original helper comparisons.
Those are separate counts, and no actual pass is preclaimed by this stage.

The additive notes-todo-experiment collector branch requires exactly that17-file
Notes census roster, each of the23 actual new TAP subtest names once, complete
summary totals with zero failure/cancellation/skip/todo, the16+4 original helper
observation, and actual HTTP client/core/markdown byte/hash delivery evidence.
Current live target and source-copy after identities must match. All other
eligible active Studio source bytes must match committed Git blobs; the full
eligible source census and active snapshots remain before/after authenticated.
Existing collection scopes, their test bodies and acceptance branches remain.

Notes dependencies are committed fixture/retained original source bytes and the
Windows runner's system TAR parser. No vendor download/bootstrap acquisition
or fixture generation is performed. Old original-notebook helper observations
remain distinct from the new20 to-do comparisons. Four existing configurable
observation writers target the evidence directory; the single hardcoded old
trash-original.json is explicitly copied with its identity after the child.

The workflow uses a narrow push trigger for the recovery branch and its own
workflow/bundle/composer paths, plus manual invocation after registration. The
standard Windows2022 job has a30-minute limit, the child a20-minute deadline,
an independent always-run exact source postcheck, and always-run evidence
packaging. A15MiB ZIP cap and one-day artifact retention match the reviewed
pattern; oversized evidence uploads only explicitly incomplete diagnostics and
fails the job. All failure/partial composition receipts must be preserved.

before/verify-cloud.mjs.snapshot now preserves the66136-byte999768d5 Vault r7 source epoch.
The authoring Python script only reads selected source/data and writes source
files; it never imports or runs candidate JavaScript. No product test, verifier,
syntax check, build, original helper/program or browser has run locally.
There is no actual Notes cloud result yet. Root/independent source review,
exact commit/push, actual hosted run, recoverable local backup and actual browser
acceptance remain pending. The source mode emits no full development receipt.
No product installation, full parity, security or superiority is established.

The previous complete21-file candidate and authority5e67f587 remain under
versions/pre-vault-r7-r1. Rebase r2 changes only the generic collector's exact
Vault bundle pin from5da77639 to b5b615aa; its Notes additions stay byte-exact.
All other20 public candidate files remain unchanged. Vault r7 changes only its
original save/reopen timestamp expectation to the source-defined whole-second
projection, preserving raw original observations and all non-time comparisons.
The Notes authority now requires that reviewed r7 collector before-image; do not
overwrite a different active collector epoch. No hosted or local execution was
performed by this rebase.
