  "review": [
    "Read the full22,945-byte initial architecture, complete2,688-byte net revised plan delta, full inventory-authoring reader and actual relevant migration/helper/collector/workflow/producer/control read sites. R2 authority files are exact and R2 inventory differs from prior independently audited89e inventory only by actual Git head. All32 current app pins,60 prospective proof pins,52 old objects and protected source pins independently match d24 immutable Git inputs.",
    "Seven exact R5 transitions produce36 app sources/34eligible sources and12 distinct targets across the old8/new7 sets. New committed111/8 workflow/helper/standalone collector avoids weakening old32 scopes or importing the old composer; old automatic contracts retire only with the same reviewed current36 replacement commit and full preserved workflow before-images.",
    "Closed groups remain independent: legacy52 historical proof, legacy56 storage envelope, newcurrent60 proof,12 tooling,common159/160,Archive94/96. Existing prospective60 rows total650,028B; replacing the14,958B experiment workflow leaves635,070B plus the externally pinned declaration. The declaration enumerates the other59, never fingerprints itself or its own pinning readers. Its literal external identity is identical in current60 and tooling12, preventing a hash cycle or arbitrary self acceptance.",
    "Exactly three legacy32 logical source reads project to pinned R5 before-images. Closed52 logical and52 physical names remain distinct and exact; legacy56 separately maps the retired installed workflow to its frozen physical alias. No generic fallback or current-path substitution is allowed. Current7 resolver precedence keeps R5after current, old32after historical, still-older pre-Todo identities on their original aliases, and rejects unknown/missing identities.",
    "Existing root/historical937/followup/inline readers already use exact expected-identity routing. Preserve their actual149,123/46,118-byte current source pins if projection suffices. Historical old8/52 summaries must be labelled historical, while fresh current36/7 are separately mandatory. Preserve208 control semantics, split replaced live versus historical mutation rejection and add meaningful new current/source/census/envelope controls; derive the new count from actual frozen rows.",
    "Predicted94 publication artifact files remain a forecast, not a proven output. Future implementation must freeze the complete exact role table under96, reject extra roles and independently enforce per-envelope row/byte limits. All new journal/old-source lineage inputs require an explicit group if used as proof.",
    "Fresh installed111/8, strict old-roster-plus19-name full suite (1119 forecast only), new source/syntax/publication checks and portable evidence readback remain mandatory after reviewed copy. Previous experimental111/8, installed32/92/8 and failed epochs do not become new installation acceptance."
